title: The metadata map
tags: [[Embedded metadata]]
kind: reference
summary: .metafolder/metadata-map.toml maps native tag names to mfr_meta_* fields with a type — per repository, seeded at init, repaired if deleted.

The same meaning is spelled differently across formats (a performer is ID3 `TPE1`,
Vorbis `ARTIST`, MP4 `©ART`), and which keys are worth keeping is a matter of taste. So
extraction follows an editable map, one `[[field]]` table per target field:

```
[[field]]
name = "artist"               # stored as mfr_meta_artist
type = "string"               # string, int, float or datetime
from = ["TrackArtist", "Artist"]
```

The extractor collects every `(source key, value)` the file provides, then writes each
field from the ''first'' key of its `from` list that is present ''and'' parses into its
type — a malformed tag is skipped for the next source, never poisoning the field. Only
these normalised fields are stored, never the hundreds of raw format-specific tags,
which would flood the field catalogue.

''Source keys'':

* audio tags — `lofty`'s normalised item keys (`TrackTitle`, `TrackArtist`, `AlbumTitle`, `AlbumArtist`, `Genre`, `RecordingDate`, `Year`, `TrackNumber`, `DiscNumber`, `Comment`…), which already unify the ID3, Vorbis and MP4 spellings; an unmapped native tag is offered under its raw name;
* image tags — EXIF/TIFF names (`DateTimeOriginal`, `Make`, `Model`, `Orientation`, `GPSLatitude`, `GPSLongitude`, `Artist`, `Copyright`…);
* stream properties — computed, not tags, so under `@` keys: `@duration_ms`, `@bitrate`, `@sample_rate`, `@channels`, `@width`, `@height`.

A `datetime` is stored as its instant: a bare year (Vorbis `DATE 1998`) becomes that year's
1 January 00:00 UTC, EXIF `DateTimeOriginal` its exact instant. Only keys the file
provides are written; the others stay unknown. All `mfr_meta_*` names are reserved
([[Reserved fields]]).

''The default map'' (`crates/daemon/src/default-metadata-map.toml`) has twenty fields:
`title`, `artist`, `album_artist` (kept distinct from `artist`, to group compilations —
merge them by adding its sources to `artist`), `album`, `genre`, `track`, `disc`, `date`
(`DateTimeOriginal`, `RecordingDate`, `Year`), `comment`, `duration`, `bitrate`,
`sample_rate`, `channels`, `width`, `height`, `camera_make`, `camera_model`, `orientation`,
`gps_lat`, `gps_lon`.

!! Where it lives

`.metafolder/metadata-map.toml`, per repository, beside `config.json` and `schema.json` —
ordinary trackable content, on the schema's model rather than the configuration
repository's: repositories in different languages or conventions want different maps, and
the map belongs with what it describes ([[Repository layout on disk]]).

* `mf repo init` seeds it from the default baked into the daemon; editing the shipped default affects new repositories only.
* At load, a ''missing'' file is written from the default, then read — repository data, not user configuration, so this is no runtime fallback. A ''malformed'' one fails that repository's load alone, never the daemon, like an invalid `schema.json`.

A newly mapped field is picked up by a file's ''next'' extraction, which needs its marker
cleared ([[When metadata is extracted]]).
